j-a0b3e1ca75.design-under-investigation.a1], or if RTL with only the outer statement removed still fails the regression. (2) testbench_bug, wrong expected value in the regression check. Rejected because the attached repro derives its expected byte (8'hA5) from the header specification, not from RTL output, and expects the second start to be ignored. Still open: I have not seen the content of the upstream uart_tx_triage_repro.v or of regression_fail.log. Refuted-against if the repro passes on the mutant but the regression still fails. (3) infrastructure. Rejected because [run:run-0002] built, reached $finish and gave a deterministic count of failed checks, with no build or tool error reported. A clean rebuild with no other change, failing identically, would close this fully. (4) spec_ambiguity. Rejected because the header clause states that a start pulse during a frame is ignored, and the natural reading is that the transmitted frame keeps its original data. Would be reopened if a separate specification says data may be re-sampled mid-frame. The repro testbench uart_tx_reload_repro_tb.v targets hypothesis (1): it should fail on the mutant and pass on fixed RTL. Whether it actually fails is for the platform's simulator.run gate to establish."}], "files": [{"path": "uart_tx_reload_repro_tb.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Self-checking repro: start pulse during DATA must not change the in-flight frame", "summary": "Minimal repro for the rtl_bug hypothesis about [artifact:prj-a0b3e1ca75.design-under-investigation.a1], serving [requirement:req-d10c4df532]. Steps: reset, send 8'hA5, then pulse start with 8'h3C during data bit 1. A mid-bit receiver checks four things against the module's specified behaviour (8N1, LSB first, start pulse while busy ignored): start bit low, received byte equals 8'hA5, stop bit high, and the line stays idle with busy low afterwards. On the reload-while-busy RTL, bits 3, 4, 6 and 7 should come from 8'h3C, so the byte check is expected to fail