Send 8'hA5.\n- Pulse start with 8'h3C during data bit 1.\n- Check the start bit, the stop bit, the received byte == 8'hA5, and that the line is idle and not busy afterwards.\n\nThe nonce acquisition is rewritten because [evidence:prj-a0b3e1ca75.root-cause.e1] showed the verdict printed 'missing'. It prints exactly one 'NIRMAAN-SIM <nonce> <n> passed, <m> failed' line. Expected to fail on the RTL under investigation and pass on RTL that ignores start while busy.", "entry": "uart_tx_reload_repro_tb"}], "tool_runs": [], "claims": ["The exact mechanism by which the platform passes the run nonce is not in my inputs. This testbench tries several plusarg names, a prefix match, and nonce files; whether any of them matches is unverified.", "The repro is expected to pass on a uart_tx that loads 'hold' only in IDLE. No such run is in the cited evidence.", "Removing the top-level 'if (start) hold <= data;' is expected to fix the failure without other changes. This has not been simulated."], "escalation": null, "notes": "Outcome rtl_bug. The diagnosis is well supported. My residual uncertainty is mostly the nonce interface that made attempt 1 fail; the diagnosis itself is not in doubt.\n\nIf this attempt again fails with a 'missing' or wrong nonce, the next step should be to read uart_tx_triage_repro.v (the triage testbench that reproduced in [run:run-0002]) with artifact.read and copy its nonce handling exactly. Failing that, escalate to verification.debug.analysis.tech_lead asking for the nonce plusarg or file convention.\n\nI ran no tools in this answer."}
